      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(52^\\circ\\right)}{\\cot\\left(26^\\circ\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(26^\\circ\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(26^\\circ\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(52^\\circ\\right)=2sc$.\n\n Also, $\\cot\\left(26^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{c}{s}$.\n\nRewrite the quotient ratio before cancelling.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc}{\\frac{c}{s}} &=2s^2 \\\\ &=2\\sin^2\\left(26^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
